      "side": 1,
      "message": "For usb_typec_vpd and usb_prl_old, I think you probably want to make your changes to fake_usbc.c. usb_sm_checks.c is used in a few other targets, and you may be getting linker errors from those targets. More importantly, fake_usbc.c is clearly made for this purpose, and usb_sm_checks.c is clearly made for a different purpose.\n\nFor usb_typec_drp_acc_trysrc, it looks like the fake mechanism is different. usb_typec_drp_acc_trysrc.mocklist contains a list of modules from common/mock that will be linked into that test. You can see some description of this mechanism in https://crrev.com/45b711edf84263ce7e7eef25f21d76ee43b755ec/common/mock/README.md.\n\nI\u0027d recommend moving your current stub to fake_usbc.c, seeing what the build does, and then seeing what you can do with mocks.",
